          "text": "CLINICAL INDICATION  \nHistory of focal epilepsy with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures, beginning at age 30 and occurring approximately once per month. Etiology is categorized as metabolic. Seizures are drug responsive. Current antiseizure medications are lacosamide and valproate.\n\nTECHNIQUE  \nRoutine scalp EEG recording using the International 10–20 electrode placement system.\n\nFINDINGS  \nNo EEG tracing or electrographic findings were provided for interpretation. Background activity, interictal epileptiform abnormalities, and ictal activity therefore cannot be assessed.\n\nIMPRESSION  \nNo electrodiagnostic interpretation can be made from the available clinical history alone. Epilepsy classification and seizure type are based on the provided clinical history, not on EEG findings.",
